    "# Motor Stall Test Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "A simple test setup to measure current draw of a 12V DC motor using a low-side shunt resistor. Data is sampled and streamed over serial to Edge Impulse for data collection and visualization.\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src = \"Day 2\Assets\circuit.png" width=\"50%\">\n", 
    "\n",
    "## Required Components\n",
    "\n",
    "- Arduino (Uno / compatible)\n",
    "- Breadboard\n",
    "- Shunt Resistor (≈ 0.1Ω – 0.5Ω recommended)\n",
    "- 12V DC Motor\n",
    "- Flyback Diode (1N4007 or similar)\n",
    "- Jumper Wires\n",
    "- External 12V Wall Adapter + Barrel Jack Connector\n",
    "- USB Cable (for Arduino)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## Circuit Overview\n",
    "<img src = \"circuit_schematic.png\" width=\"50%\">\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Notes:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- The shunt resistor is placed on the **low side** (between motor and GND)\n",
    "- Arduino GND **must** be shared with the motor power supply GND\n",
    "- The flyback diode **must** be wired in parallel with the motor and the stripe always faces the positive side of the power supply\n",
    "- The stripe from the flyback diode represents the arrow that shows which way the current is allowed to flow through\n",
    "- The ADC pin measures the voltage across the shunt resistor\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## Setup Instructions\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Wire the Circuit\n",
    "\n",
    "- You can easily use your fingernails to strip the wires for the motor, since they're quite thin. Press your thumbnail all around the circumference of the wire then pull hard to pull out the insulation.\n",
    "- Double-check all connections before powering on.\n",
    "- Use the 12V wall adapter and connect it to the nearest wall outlet.\n",
    "- Use the barrel jack connector to connect the wall adapter to your breadboard.\n",
    "- Using the wires screwed into the barrel jack connector, follow the circuit diagram to supply power to your breadboard.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Upload Arduino Code\n",
    "\n",
    "Upload the code in [motor_data_collection.ino](motor_data_collection/motor_data_collection.ino) using Arduino IDE\n",
    "\n",
    "**Troubleshooting Upload Errors:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- If you see any upload errors (e.g., Exit 74):\n",
    "  - Go to **Tools** -> **Reload Board Data**\n",
    "  - Then double-press the RESET (on the arduino) button to enter bootloader mode\n",
    "  - Retry upload\n",
    "\n",
    "Close the Serial Monitor before uploading.\n",
    "\n",
    "After uploading, close the Arduino IDE.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Stalling Tips\n",
    "\n",
    "- To stall the motor, you can hold on to the shaft using your fingers. You can also ask for pliers at the front, if you need.\n",
    "- You might want one person to hold on to the motor stand's base to keep it stable while stalling, so it doesn't topple and also to get better readings while sampling data.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Safety Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "- Do **not** exceed the motor’s rated voltage.\n",
    "- Do **NOT** stall the motor for more than 2 seconds — it can draw high current.\n",
    "- Be careful when stalling the motor.\n",
    "- If you find the motor getting warm/hot, disconnect the barrel jack connector from the wall adapter to let it cool off.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
